# Audit logging direction

Saqr is **gradually replacing** the custom `AuditLogEntry` / Accounting → Audit log style with the **`audited` gem** (`Audited::Audit`).

## Prefer

- New change-tracking on models → `audited` (with `associated_with: :company` when tenant-scoped)
- Per-record history UI → show-page panels backed by `@record.audits` (see `shared/audit_history`)
- Extending `audited` coverage to more models over time (expenses, incomes, users already done)

## Avoid (unless explicitly asked)

- Adding new `AuditLogEntry.record!` call sites for ordinary create/update/destroy history
- Building new features around the Accounting Audit log as the long-term home for model change history
- Dual-writing the same event to both systems without a migration plan

## Current coexistence (intentional for now)

- `AuditLogEntry` still powers Accounting → Audit log for JE/payments/shifts/reversal *events*
- `Audited::Audit` powers field-level history on expense / income / staff show pages
- Do **not** do a big-bang migration unless the user asks; when touching audit-related code, nudge toward `audited` and do not expand `AuditLogEntry` usage
